.TH UPDATE-NOTIFY-CAA 1 "August 2026" "mu2edaq-notify 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
update\-notify\-caa.sh \- bind certificate issuance for the proxy's name to one CA and ACME account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./scripts/update\-notify\-caa.sh
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
[\fB\-\-remove\fR]
[\fB\-\-account\-uri\fR \fIURI\fR]...
[\fB\-\-all\-accounts\fR]
[\fB\-\-ca\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-validation\-methods\fR \fILIST\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-issuewild\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fIRECORD\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR \fIZONE_ID\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-H\fR \fIHOST\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Publishes, checks or removes the
.B CAA
record set on
.B notify.andrewnorman.org
that restricts who may obtain a certificate for the name: RFC 8659 for the
.B issue
and
.B issuewild
tags, RFC 8657 for the
.B accounturi
and
.B validationmethods
parameters. Let's Encrypt has enforced both parameters in production since
December 2022.
.PP
The written record set is, by default:
.PP
.RS
.nf
0 issue "letsencrypt.org;accounturi=<URI>;validationmethods=http\-01,tls\-alpn\-01"
0 issuewild ";"
.fi
.RE
.SH WHY
The proxy holds no Elastic IP. A stopped instance returns its public address to
the AWS pool, so whoever is handed that address next controls ports 80 and 443
on it and can satisfy an HTTP\-01 or TLS\-ALPN\-01 challenge for the name \(en
which would let them serve trusted TLS as
.B notify.andrewnorman.org
to enrolling phones.
.PP
Retracting the
.B A
record at teardown closes the window
.RB ( update-notify-dns.sh (1)
.BR \-\-retract ).
This closes the hole itself: with
.B accounturi
set, possession of the address is no longer sufficient \(en the ACME account key
is needed too, and that never leaves the instance.
.PP
.B issuewild ";"
denies wildcard issuance outright, because this name never needs one and a
wildcard is the certificate an attacker would most want.
.SH THE ACCOUNT URI
Read off the instance rather than configured, because Caddy creates the account,
not the operator. The script searches Caddy's storage for account JSON under
.IR /var/lib/caddy ,
.I /root/.local/share/caddy
and
.IR /home/*/.local/share/caddy ,
extracts every
.I https://acme\-.../acme/acct/N
it finds, drops staging accounts, and refuses to guess if more than one remains
\(en pinning the wrong one blocks renewal. The instance must be running.
.PP
.B A rebuilt instance means a new account.
Caddy registers a fresh one when its storage is empty, and the old pin then
forbids issuance. Caddy renews at two thirds of the 90\-day lifetime, so the
failure surfaces weeks after the rebuild, not at boot. Re\-run this script as
part of any rebuild, and check it with
.B \-\-check
after one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Compare the live record against the instance's account and change nothing.
Exits 1 when the record is missing or does not authorize that account, so it
works as a monitoring probe.
.TP
.B \-\-remove
Delete the record set. The escape hatch for an over\-tight record; it rebuilds
the
.B DELETE
from the live values rather than from what this run would have written, because
Route 53 requires a delete to match exactly.
.TP
.B \-\-account\-uri \fIURI\fR
Authorize this account instead of asking the instance. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-accounts
Authorize every account found on the instance instead of refusing when there is
more than one.
.TP
.B \-\-ca \fIDOMAIN\fR
CA identifier. Default
.BR letsencrypt.org ,
matching the
.B acme_ca
pin in
.IR config/aws/Caddyfile .
Change both together.
.TP
.B \-\-validation\-methods \fILIST\fR
RFC 8657
.BR validationmethods ,
comma separated. Default
.BR http\-01,tls\-alpn\-01 ,
the two challenges Caddy uses here; this also forbids
.BR dns\-01 ,
so it would have to be widened before any wildcard or DNS\-challenge
configuration. An empty value omits the parameter.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-issuewild
Do not write the wildcard denial.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-record " " \fIRECORD\fR
Record to pin. Writing CAA at the zone apex is refused outright: it would apply
to every name in the zone without its own CAA, including ones served by ACM
certificates, and that breakage would only appear at their next renewal.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zone " " \fIZONE_ID\fR
Hosted zone. Default
.BR Z2OL4WKH228GKD .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-ttl " " \fISECONDS\fR
Record TTL, default 300. Only CAs read this record, and only at issuance.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " " \fIHOST\fR, \fB\-u\fR \fIUSER\fR, \fB\-k\fR \fIFILE\fR
SSH target, user and key for account discovery. The address defaults to the
instance's current one from the EC2 API.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-wait
Do not poll the change to
.BR INSYNC .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the change batch, submit nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CAA_CA,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CAA_VALIDATION_METHODS,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CAA_TTL,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_DNS_NAME,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_ROUTE53_ZONE_ID,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_USER,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_KEY.
.SH PERMISSIONS
Only the operator writes this record. The instance's own IAM policy
.RI ( config/aws/notify\-dns\-role.cfn.yaml )
is limited to
.B UPSERT
of the
.B A
record and deliberately cannot touch
.BR CAA ,
so a compromised proxy cannot widen its own issuance policy.
.SH EXAMPLES
Publish the pin, reading the account off the running instance:
.PP
.RS
.nf
scripts/update\-notify\-caa.sh
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify it after a rebuild, and see what is live:
.PP
.RS
.nf
scripts/update\-notify\-caa.sh \-\-check
dig +short notify.andrewnorman.org CAA
.fi
.RE
.PP
Back it out if it is blocking renewal:
.PP
.RS
.nf
scripts/update\-notify\-caa.sh \-\-remove
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR update-notify-dns.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq-notify-dns-update (1),
.BR install-notify-dns-updater.sh (1),
.IR docs/reverse\-proxy\-setup.md
.PP
Let's Encrypt CAA documentation: https://letsencrypt.org/docs/caa/
